<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n51223" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vīvax</span></b> , ācis,
			adj.
		vivo. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Tenacious of life</i>, <i>long-lived</i>, <i>vivacious</i> (<b>poet.</b>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">phoenix,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					Am. 2, 6, 54</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">anus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					M. 13, 519</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">patrem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. F.
					2, 625</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mater,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					S. 2, 1, 53</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cervus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					E. 7, 30</span></i>
			 Forbig. ad loc.; <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 3, 194</span></i>; <i><span class="en">7, 273</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sibylla,</span>”
				<i>ancient</i>, <i>venerable</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 14, 104</span></i>
			 (cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lux aeterna,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 14, 132</span></i>
			).—<i>Comp.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">heres,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					S. 2, 2, 132</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, of things, concr. and abstr., <i>lasting long</i>, <i>enduring</i>,
				<i>durable</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">apium (opp. breve lilium),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					C. 1, 36, 16</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">oliva,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					G. 2, 181</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vivaci cespite,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. F.
					4, 397</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gratia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor. A.
					P. 69</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">virtus expersque sepulcri,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					P. 4, 8, 47</span></i>
			.— 
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Lively</i>, <i>vigorous</i>, <i>vivacious</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sulfura,</span>”
				<i>burning briskly</i>, <i>inflammable</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					3, 374</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">solum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 1, 420</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vivacissimus cursus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell.
					5, 2, 4</span></i>
			: discipuli paulo vivaciores, <i>more
			lively</i>, <i>brisker</i>, <i>quick</i>, <i>eager</i>, = alacriores, <i><span class="en">Quint. 2, 6,
				3</span></i> Spald.—<i>Adv.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vīvācĭter</span></b> , <i>with liveliness</i> or <i>spirit</i>, <i>vigorously</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pertractare res mysticas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Fulg. Myth. 1 praef.</span></i>
			
			<i>med.; comp.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vivacius quaerere abdita,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prud. adv. Symm. 2, 332</span></i>
			.</div>
